# gh-app-token accounts. An example: it does nothing until you copy it.
#
# The gh wrapper in ~/.local/bin reads ~/.config/gh-app-token/apps (no
# .example) to give coding agents a GitHub App token for the account that owns
# the repository they are working on. See "GitHub App tokens for coding
# agents" in SETUP.md for creating the Apps and the 1Password items.
#
# One line per GitHub account (a user or an organization) that has its own
# App installed:
#
#   <owner><TAB><1Password item reference>
#
# The reference is op://<vault>/<item>, without a field. The item holds three
# fields: app_id, installation_id and private_key (the App's .pem file).
#
# The first line is the default account. Its App is used for repositories of
# any owner not listed here, and for calls with no repository at all.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. Replace both lines below with your own.
example-org	op://Example Vault/example-org GitHub App
example-user	op://Example Vault/example-user GitHub App
